From f55c0bbd8b6c5bac7b22128c53bbcad8797e2807 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kirill <sleeply4cat@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 03:12:13 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] serial: keep going when SERIAL_PROBE_ALL can't probe a
 port

One serial port that fails to probe stopped U-Boot with no console at
all, before the environment could pick a working one. Warn about the
port and go on. On SM6225 the Bluetooth UART fails, its pinctrl state
names a function the pinctrl driver doesn't know.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015ya7ejvazDaFBN5SE4ttFx
---
 drivers/serial/serial-uclass.c | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/serial/serial-uclass.c b/drivers/serial/serial-uclass.c
index 9be2ad27..7ba4711d 100644
--- a/drivers/serial/serial-uclass.c
+++ b/drivers/serial/serial-uclass.c
@@ -233,11 +233,14 @@ int serial_initialize(void)
 {
 	/* Scanning uclass to probe devices */
 	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_SERIAL_PROBE_ALL)) {
+		struct udevice *dev;
 		int ret;
 
-		ret  = uclass_probe_all(UCLASS_SERIAL);
-		if (ret)
-			return ret;
+		/* A port that fails to probe is no reason to stop with no console at all */
+		for (ret = uclass_first_device_check(UCLASS_SERIAL, &dev); dev;
+		     ret = uclass_next_device_check(&dev))
+			if (ret)
+				printf("%s: probe failed: %d\n", dev->name, ret);
 	}
 
 	return serial_init();
-- 
